sysible-branding (0.1.2) sysible; urgency=medium

  * detect the legacy patched gnome-shell-theme.gresource and say so. Until
    547444b (1 Sep 2026) apply-login-background compiled the greeter background
    INTO that resource, kept no backup, and skipped its own work when it found
    the resource already present. Machines installed from an earlier ISO still
    paint the greeter from it, so shipping a new sysible-login.png cannot reach
    them — the greeter never reads the file. Reported as the greeter still
    showing "ENGINEERING · AUTOMATION" after an upgrade that had already put
    "· CLOUD" on the desktop wallpaper.
  * the script does not repair it: restoring the stock resource needs apt, which
    cannot run inside a dpkg transaction, and rebuilding the gresource is what
    547444b removed because a bad rebuild wedges the greeter on some GPUs. It
    prints the one command that fixes it, to stderr and to the journal:
        sudo apt install --reinstall gnome-shell-common && sudo reboot

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:20:00 +0000

sysible-branding (0.1.1) sysible; urgency=medium

  * redesign GDM login background: drop the centered S-mark (it overlapped the login dialog) and shrink the wordmark to a small bottom footer

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Thu, 13 Aug 2026 02:45:48 +0000

sysible-branding (0.1.0) sysible; urgency=medium

  * Initial package: ships the SES brand assets that were previously only baked
    into the ISO (GRUB theme, GDM login background, Sysible app icons, Sora
    font). postinst re-applies them (update-grub, login gresource, icon/font
    caches) on install and upgrade so brand changes flow via apt.

 -- Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:31:37 +0000
